# The Buffalo lectures (1973), in Lean

Alexander Grothendieck's lectures at SUNY Buffalo in 1973 (algebraic geometry, algebraic groups,
topos theory), as indexed in our own words in `docs/buffalo-ag/index.tex`,
`docs/buffalo-groupes/index.tex` and `docs/buffalo-topos/index.tex`. Each file
`Buffalo/<Course>/PartNN.lean` takes a run of consecutive entries of one index and, for each,
either proves it, points to the Mathlib declaration that is it, or proves it false when the
index got it wrong. The status of every entry is in `docs/buffalo-<course>/lean.json`.

A proof here says that the index's statement holds together, not that it is what was said at the
blackboard.
